        "id": 11413,
        "name": "robbritt",
        "username": "robbritt",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/b487fb/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-15T16:34:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1) I have a card that says \"at the beginning of the villain phase, draw a card from the villain deck.\"&nbsp; A number of cards say something like that, so the specific one doesn't really matter.&nbsp; The card I draw says \"at the beginning of the villain phase, do XYZ\".&nbsp; Do I do XYZ on the same turn I drew the card?&nbsp; Are we still in the beginning of the villain phase, or did that end when I followed all the directions on the card that I already had in hand?&nbsp;</p><p>Is this true for all \"beginning of\"/\"end of\" directions?&nbsp; Now, if you draw a card at the beginning of the phase that says do something at the end, I would think you would do it on the same turn.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2) If I'm in a situation where I'm supposed to apply damage or healing to the hero with highest/lowest hit points, and I have a tie, do they both take damage or get healed?&nbsp; Do the players get to decide which one?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thank you.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:43.098Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
