      {
        "id": 119390,
        "name": "grysqrl",
        "username": "grysqrl",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/{size}/1909_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-15T16:44:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1) Start-of-turn effects played during the start-of-turn phase take effect that turn. End-of-turn effects played during the end-of-turn phase also take effect that turn. You process start- and end-of-turn effects in the order in which they entered play. Any new effect necessarily enters play after the card that caused it to enter play, so it still has a chance to be processed. The only exception (and this isn't really an exception) is start-of-turn effects that enter play after the start-of-turn phase; at this point, start-of-turn effects are no longer being processed, so the new one won't take effect until the next turn.</p><p>2) One of them will take the damage/healing. Players choose how to break the tie.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:52:34.113Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
