        "raw": "<p>1) Start-of-turn effects played during the start-of-turn phase take effect that turn. End-of-turn effects played during the end-of-turn phase also take effect that turn. You process start- and end-of-turn effects in the order in which they entered play. Any new effect necessarily enters play after the card that caused it to enter play, so it still has a chance to be processed. The only exception (and this isn&#39;t really an exception) is start-of-turn effects that enter play after the start-of-turn phase; at this point, start-of-turn effects are no longer being processed, so the new one won&#39;t take effect until the next turn.</p><p>2) One of them will take the damage/healing. Players choose how to break the tie.</p>",
